,"name":"Electronics","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"2079-9292","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.3390/electronics12040969","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics12040969","citation_count":11,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.3390/electronics12040969","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/electronics12040969","query":"deep learning image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:33:01Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-91cca5a144d6498f","title":"Deepfake noise investigation and detection","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"2022-07-01","abstract":"The fast development of Deepfake has brought huge current and potential future negative impacts to our daily lives. As the circulating popular Deepfake videos have become difficult to be distinguished by human eyes, various Deepfake detection approaches have been attempted using deep learning models. However, even though some existing detection methods have achieved reasonable detection performance with respect to the statistical evaluation metrics, the actual underlying Deepfake forensic traces have been barely discussed. In this study, we investigate the special forensic noise traces within Deepfake image frames and propose a noise-based Deepfake detection model approach using a deep neural network. We train a Siamese noise extractor using a novel face-background strategy to investigate different forensic noise traces of a synthesized face area and an unmodified background area. A similarity matrix module is proposed to analyze the forensic noise trace difference between a cropped face square and a cropped background square from a candidate image frame for the Deepfake detection task. As a result, our proposed model trained on the high-quality Celeb-DF dataset has achieved state-of-the-art performance with 99.15% accuracy and 99.92% AUC score on the in-dataset testing set and 88.95% AUC score on the highly difficult unknown-attack Deepfake video dataset. Furthermore, the visualization of the Deepfake forensic noise traces has shown the explicit distinction between synthesized faces and any unmodified area. We believe that the visualized evidence could provide better proof of Deepfake detection results rather than simply the statistical evaluation numbers.","authors":[{"id":"a5100399645","name":"Tianyi Wang","orcid":"0000-0003-2920-6099","institution_ids":["i889458895"]},{"id":"a5038738776","name":"Ming Liu","orcid":"0000-0003-0985-0768","institution_ids":["i152269853","i4210142748"]},{"id":"a5079314368","name":"Wei Cao","orcid":"0000-0002-4723-4715","institution_ids":["i152269853","i4210142748"]},{"id":"a5040488307","name":"K. P. Chow","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i889458895"]}],"institution_ids":["i152269853","i4210142748","i889458895"],"venue":{"id":"venue-16b5f189aace76","name":"Forensic Science International Digital Investigation","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["deepfake_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1016/j.fsidi.2022.301395","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4284964929","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fsidi.2022.301395","citation_count":28,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4284964929","url":"https://openalex.org/W4284964929","query":"deepfake image forensics","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-7420ce7a27d51c8f","title":"Image Forgery Detection via Forensic Similarity Graphs","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-8ce44fb1959d33","name":"Marina Gardella","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-a673aa8ce807e8","name":"Pablo Musé","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-b2b3b940b90ec6","name":"Image Processing On Line","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"2105-1232","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.5201/ipol.2022.432","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.5201/ipol.2022.432","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.5201/ipol.2022.432","url":"https://doi.org/10.5201/ipol.2022.432","query":"scene text image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:29:54Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-14d3ef1aea75f98f","title":"SISL:Self-Supervised Image Signature Learning for Splicing Detection &amp; Localization","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"2022-06-01","abstract":"Recent algorithms for image manipulation detection almost exclusively use deep network models. These approaches require either dense pixelwise groundtruth masks, camera ids, or image metadata to train the networks. On one hand, constructing a training set to represent the countless tampering possibilities is impractical. On the other hand, social media platforms or commercial applications are often constrained to remove camera ids as well as metadata from images. A self-supervised algorithm for training manipulation detection models without dense groundtruth or camera/image metadata would be extremely useful for many forensics applications. In this paper, we propose a self-supervised approach for training splicing detection/localization models from frequency transform of images. To identify the spliced regions, our deep network learns a representation to capture an image-specific signature by enforcing (image) self consistency. We experimentally demonstrate that our proposed model can yield similar or better performances as compared to multiple existing methods on standard datasets without relying on labels or metadata.","authors":[{"id":"a5026783028","name":"Susmit Agrawal","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i59270414"]},{"id":"a5026462797","name":"Prabhat Kumar","orcid":"0000-0001-9945-7702","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5072987937","name":"Siddharth Seth","orcid":"0000-0002-4481-8504","institution_ids":["i4210112936"]},{"id":"a5062468877","name":"Toufiq Parag","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i4210112936"]},{"id":"a5101827826","name":"Maneesh Singh","orcid":"0000-0003-0901-3388","institution_ids":["i4210112936"]},{"id":"a5033240172","name":"Venkatesh Babu","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i59270414"]}],"institution_ids":["i4210112936","i59270414"],"venue":{"id":"venue-d07a658b0594f9","name":"2022 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops (CVPRW)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/cvprw56347.2022.00012","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4292794770","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/cvprw56347.2022.00012","citation_count":15,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4292794770","url":"https://openalex.org/W4292794770","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-a81be0f1f46d888f","title":"Copy Move Forgery Detection in Digital Images and Their Analysis: -A Review","title_zh":"","year":2021,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-a57a1f2cec41b7","name":"Smriti Guleria","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-f4288f3da9b8ae","name":"Mandeep Kaur","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-c21bcf90e69393","name":"SSRN Electronic Journal","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"1556-5068","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"survey","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.2139/ssrn.3852505","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.3852505","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.2139/ssrn.3852505","url":"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.3852505","query":"copy move image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:42Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-1f7d088843c5898f","title":"Deep Learning on Digital Image Splicing Detection Using CFA Artifacts","title_zh":"","year":2020,"publication_date":"2020-02-14","abstract":"Digital image forgery is a serious problem of an increasing attention from the research society. Image splicing is a well-known type of digital image forgery in which the forged image is synthesized from two or more images. Splicing forgery detection is more challenging when compared with other forgery types because the forged image does not contain any duplicated regions. In addition, unavailability of source images introduces no evidence about the forgery process. In this study, an automated image splicing forgery detection scheme is presented. It depends on extracting the feature of images based on the analysis of color filter array (CFA). A feature reduction process is performed using principal component analysis (PCA) to reduce the dimensionality of the resulting feature vectors. A deep belief network-based classifier is built and trained to classify the tested images as authentic or spliced images. The proposed scheme is evaluated through a set of experiments on Columbia Image Splicing Detection Evaluation Dataset (CISDED) under different scenarios including adding postprocessing on the spliced images such JPEG compression and Gaussian Noise. The obtained results reveal that the proposed scheme exhibits a promising performance with 95.05% precision, 94.05% recall, 94.05% true positive rate, and 98.197% accuracy. Moreover, the obtained results show the superiority of the proposed scheme compared to other recent splicing detection method.","authors":[{"id":"a5057572474","name":"Nadheer Younus Hussien","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i207547235"]},{"id":"a5108819055","name":"Rasha Orban Mahmoud","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i207547235"]},{"id":"a5044492187","name":"Hala H. Zayed","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-7577","institution_ids":["i207547235"]}],"institution_ids":["i207547235"],"venue":{"id":"venue-823d56f76c2adc","name":"International Journal of Sociotechnology and Knowledge Development","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.4018/ijskd.2020040102","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3005756777","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.4018/ijskd.2020040102","citation_count":20,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3005756777","url":"https://openalex.org/W3005756777","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.4018/ijskd.2020040102","url":"https://doi.org/10.4018/ijskd.2020040102","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:44Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-97a14bbf8918688f","title":"Digital image forgery detection based on shadow texture features","title_zh":"","year":2016,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-cfe7b774d69245","name":"Ira Tuba","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-629162a4ff753b","name":"Eva Tuba","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-14ff0d391f2c3b","name":"Marko Beko","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-e40a3555e08f22","name":"2016 24th Telecommunications Forum (TELFOR)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/telfor.2016.7818875","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/telfor.2016.7818875","citation_count":5,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/telfor.2016.7818875","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/telfor.2016.7818875","query":"image forgery detection localization","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:38Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-7669189ab2c6798f","title":"MDE-based image steganography with large embedding capacity","title_zh":"","year":2015,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5035489942","name":"Zhaoxia Yin","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-a87c0271accdc8","name":"Bin Luo","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-c2cec5c5bca959","name":"Security and Communication Networks","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"1939-0114","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1002/sec.1275","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/sec.1275","citation_count":6,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1002/sec.1275","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/sec.1275","query":"image steganography detection benchmark","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:03Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-cd55e6c8fa804a8f","title":"Image Tampering Detection and Repairing","title_zh":"","year":2014,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-4e2d5414cc35f4","name":"Jyoti Rao","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-d52b031f628985","name":"Sarika Jankar","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-41338dfd7303b2","name":"Ashwini Jarali","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-db9fff16c4bcb0","name":"International Journal of Computer Applications","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"0975-8887","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.5120/14932-3468","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.5120/14932-3468","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.5120/14932-3468","url":"https://doi.org/10.5120/14932-3468","query":"document image text tampering detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:29:58Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-589d6ed4be54778f","title":"A cost-effective decision tree based approach to steganalysis","title_zh":"","year":2013,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-853c6469811e0c","name":"Liyun Li","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5086101517","name":"Husrev Taha Sencar","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5006172625","name":"Nasir Memon","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-8d994985ad436f","name":"SPIE Proceedings","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"0277-786X","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1117/12.2008527","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.2008527","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1117/12.2008527","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.2008527","query":"image steganalysis @ USENIX Security","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:43:27Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-f5cdced282e31c8f","title":"Going from small to large data in steganalysis","title_zh":"","year":2012,"publication_date":"2012-02-08","abstract":"With most image steganalysis traditionally based on supervised machine learning methods, the size of training data has remained static at up to 20000 training examples. This potentially leads to the classifier being undertrained for larger feature sets and it may be too narrowly focused on characteristics of a source of cover images, resulting in degradation in performance when the testing source is mismatched or heterogeneous. However it is not difficult to obtain larger training sets for steganalysis through simply taking more photos or downloading additional images. Here, we investigate possibilities for creating steganalysis classifiers trained on large data sets using large feature vectors. With up to 1.6 million examples, naturally simpler classification engines must be used and we examine the hypothesis that simpler classifiers avoid overtraining and so perform better on heterogeneous data. We highlight the possibilities of online learners, showing that, when given sufficient training data, they can match or exceed the performance of complex classifiers such as Support Vector Machines. This applies to both their accuracy and training time. We include some experiments, not previously reported in the literature, which provide benchmarks of some known feature sets and classifier combinations.","authors":[{"id":"a5017913001","name":"Ivans Lubenko","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i40120149"]},{"id":"a5111728681","name":"Andrew D. Ker","orcid":"0000-0002-1154-3305","institution_ids":["i40120149"]}],"institution_ids":["i40120149"],"venue":{"id":"venue-28757b3c57cb1d","name":"Proceedings of SPIE, the International Society for Optical Engineering/Proceedings of SPIE","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1117/12.910214","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2036904261","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.910214","citation_count":32,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2036904261","url":"https://openalex.org/W2036904261","query":"cover source mismatch image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"fc296f41063f27d9a073803a2361a832e22b0595","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/fc296f41063f27d9a073803a2361a832e22b0595","query":"cover source mismatch image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:11:07Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1117/12.910214","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.910214","query":"image steganalysis @ USENIX Security","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:43:27Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-1bbc03d56cbb7e8f","title":"Steganography and Steganalysis : Different Approaches","title_zh":"","year":2012,"publication_date":"2012-01-01","abstract":"Steganography is the technique of hiding confidential information within any media. Steganography is often confused with cryptography because the two are similar in the way that they both are used to protect confidential information. The difference between the two is in the appearance in the processed output; the output of steganography operation is not apparently visible but in cryptography the output is scrambled so that it can draw attention. Steganlysis is process to detect of presence of steganography. In this article we have tried to elucidate the different approaches towards implementation of steganography using ‘multimedia’ file (text, static image, audio and video) and Network IP datagram as cover. Also some methods of steganalysis will be discussed.","authors":[{"id":"a5001455581","name":"Vinay A. Rajgure","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i150513749"]},{"id":"a5110736715","name":"Vishwas T. Gaikwad","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i150513749"]}],"institution_ids":["i150513749"],"venue":{"id":"venue-6cc07f45a61192","name":"International Journal of Electronics Signals and Systems","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.47893/ijess.2012.1032","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3120505886","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"http://doi.org/10.47893/ijess.2012.1032","citation_count":39,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3120505886","url":"https://openalex.org/W3120505886","query":"image steganalysis detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-d2f47af711a2118f","title":"Improved Weighted Stego Image Steganalysis","title_zh":"","year":2010,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5029455813","name":"Rainer Böhme","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-1b30970400764a","name":"Information Security and Cryptography","short_name":"","type":"unknown","issn":"1619-7100","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-14313-7_6","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-14313-7_6","citation_count":2,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1007/978-3-642-14313-7_6","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-14313-7_6","query":"image steganalysis detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:17:03Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-72c3c7b522c8598f","title":"Improving embedding capacity with minimum degradation of stego-image","title_zh":"","year":2008,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-6b3b9642a9aceb","name":"Sheheryar Malik","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-5805ddac2b9da9","name":"Tasneem M. Shah","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-a36052b5798960","name":"Zohaib Z. Iqbal","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-14e7e6a29180ee","name":"2008 International Symposium on Biometrics and Security Technologies","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/isbast.2008.4547658","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/isbast.2008.4547658","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/isbast.2008.4547658","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/isbast.2008.4547658","query":"cover stego image classification","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:33:14Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：